task: intent-uk-pl-rows
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/intent-uk-pl-rows
worktree: ../okay-wt-ukpl

why: owed to a consumer, promised twice and unwritten. Their
  marketplace runs in Ukrainian and Polish among others, and the
  parallel fixture has six languages, neither of them. Without those
  rows they cannot test their languages against these tiers at all,
  and CharGrams — the tier that ships and claims to be
  language-agnostic BY CONSTRUCTION — has never seen a Slavic language
  with Latin script or a second Cyrillic one.

honesty, stated up front and to be repeated in the Results: these
  rows are MY writing, which is the same disease intent-second-author
  measured. They are worth adding because a native-language consumer
  can CORRECT them, which is a thing a fixture row can be, and because
  the per-language numbers they produce are diagnostic even when the
  prose is imperfect.

what: uk and pl for all 30 parallel meanings; measure per language
  through the shipped tiers; report what CharGrams does with a Latin
  Slavic language and a second Cyrillic one; say plainly which rows a
  native speaker should look at first.

files: okay-intent/src/test/scala/okay/intent/IntentFixture.scala,
  a JVM measurement suite, specs/intent-classify.md, BACKLOG.md
